-Since the OpenBook removal an AMM v4 swap no longer validates any market state, so a V1 `SwapBaseIn` is markedly cheaper than it used to be — and `SwapBaseInV2` (8 accounts, no market placeholders) is cheaper still. Measure your own path rather than budgeting off historical figures, and always pass an explicit compute-unit limit:
